= Appendix G — Model Answers

== G.1 Distinguishing movement terms
*Question:* Explain flexion and extension at the elbow.  
*Model:* Flexion bends the elbow and reduces the angle between the upper arm and forearm; extension straightens it and increases that angle.  
*Half-answer:* “They are joint movements” names the category but does not distinguish them.

== G.2 Training principles
*Question:* Explain specificity using a running example.  
*Model:* Training adaptations relate to the demands imposed. A runner seeking improved endurance might include appropriately planned sustained running, with gradual progression and recovery.  
*Half-answer:* “Training makes you fit” does not connect the training demand to the goal.

== G.3 Inclusion
*Question:* Give one way to support participation in a target game.  
*Model:* Discuss needs with the learner and adjust the target height or distance where appropriate; then check that participation is meaningful and safe.  
*Half-answer:* “Change the game” does not say how or why.

== G.4 Pulse calculation
*Question:* Estimate the pulse rate from 17 beats in 15 seconds.  
*Model:* Multiply 17 by 4 to estimate 68 beats per minute. The estimate assumes the count represents the minute.  
*Half-answer:* “17 beats” omits the required time conversion.
